# Single Concept Aggregator Example
# Demonstrates a simple aggregator from one concept to the same concept
# using division to produce a unitless identity expression.
#
# Dimensional check:
#
#   Expression: Country/Country — postfix: Country, Country, /
#     Country/Country → unitless (cancels out)
#
#   From: {Numerator: [Country]}
#   From*Expr: {Numerator: [Country]} * unitless = {Numerator: [Country]} ✓
#   To: {Numerator: [Country]} ✓
#
# The expression Country/Country evaluates to unitless dimensional units.
# When multiplied by the input metric's units ({Numerator: [Country]}),
# the result is {Numerator: [Country]}, matching the output.
# This is effectively a no-op aggregator that preserves the Country dimension unchanged.

concepts
    Country = [Values[USA, Canada, Mexico]]

aggregators
    from [Country] to [Country] = Country/Country
